TITLE:: Sympathy
summary:: a bank of six tuned resonators that ring in a chord when the sound touches them, as a UGen and as an object, with a window
categories:: Libraries>Sympathy
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/SympathyView, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
Six tuned voices that ring when the sound touches them - hold a piano's pedal down and shout into it - running anywhere a UGen does, with a window.

code::
Ndef(\drums, { Sympathy.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(2), 0.002, 0.05) * PinkNoise.ar(0.6 ! 2), \sympathy) }).play;

y = Sympathy(Ndef(\drums), \sympathy);
y.gui;
y.root = 48; y.chord = \min9;
y.decay = 6; y.bright = 0.7;
y.tune(1, 7, 0.8);                // the second voice a fifth above the root, at 80%
y.preset = 'gamelan';
::

Each voice is six resonators tuned to the harmonics of a note: code::inharm:: stretches them as a stiff string's are, and the high ones ring for less time as code::bright:: comes down. What comes in sets them going, and they answer in the chord.

A voice is a distance from code::root:: in semitones, code::note1..6::, and a level, code::level1..6::, which has no knob: drag it on the keyboard, or use code::tune::. code::chord:: sets all six at once, from the names in code::Sympathy.chordNames::, and is a command rather than a setting, so a preset holds the notes it made.

Their level follows the input, so a long decay on a steady input gets loud, and they are limited softly on the way out. Measured on one hit of noise, code::decay:: is the time to about 60 dB down.

It is 72 code::Ringz:: at stereo, and about 3% of one core on an M4 Pro.

subsection:: The object and the UGen
It is an link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, so everything that class documents works here: code::Sympathy.ar(in, name)::, code::Sympathy(node, name)::, code::Sympathy.onBus(bus, numChannels)::, presets, the clipboard, code::gui::. Its window's display is a link::Classes/SympathyView::.

subsection:: Parameters
Each is a property of the object: read it, set it. The numbers are in the order of the node's control, which is what saved node maps carry. Internal ones without a knob, if any, are described above.

table::
## strong::parameter:: || strong::range:: || strong::default:: || strong::what it does::
## code::root:: || 24 .. 84 midi || 48 || the note everything is counted from
## code::note1:: || -24 .. 36 st || 0 || voice 1, in semitones from the root
## code::note2:: || -24 .. 36 st || 7 || voice 2, in semitones from the root
## code::note3:: || -24 .. 36 st || 12 || voice 3, in semitones from the root
## code::note4:: || -24 .. 36 st || 19 || voice 4, in semitones from the root
## code::note5:: || -24 .. 36 st || 24 || voice 5, in semitones from the root
## code::note6:: || -24 .. 36 st || 31 || voice 6, in semitones from the root
## code::glide:: || 0 .. 1 s || 0.05 || how long a voice takes to reach a new note
## code::decay:: || 0.05 .. 30 s || 3 || how long the lowest harmonic rings
## code::bright:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.5 || how long the high harmonics ring, against the low ones
## code::inharm:: || 0 .. 0.02 || 0 || the harmonics stretched sharp, as on a stiff string
## code::detune:: || 0 .. 50 c || 4 || the sides apart, in cents: slow beating
## code::vibrato:: || 0 .. 1 || 0 || how far each voice wanders, at most a semitone
## code::vibratoRate:: || 0.05 .. 12 Hz || 3 || how quickly
## code::hiCut:: || 200 .. 20000 Hz || 12000 || a low pass on what goes in
## code::loCut:: || 20 .. 2000 Hz || 40 || a high pass on what goes in
## code::input:: || -24 .. 24 dB || 0 || how hard it is played
## code::width:: || 0 .. 2 || 1 || how far apart the sides are
## code::mix:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.6 || how much of the effect goes out, against the dry signal
## code::output:: || -36 .. 24 dB || 0 || the level of the whole thing, in dB
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: chordNames
the chords by name.

METHOD:: chords
the chords, as semitones from the root.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: chord
six voices at once, by name: a setter only.

METHOD:: tune
one voice, from 0, either or both.
ARGUMENT:: voice
ARGUMENT:: semitones
ARGUMENT:: level

METHOD:: voiceNote
what a voice sounds at, in midi.
ARGUMENT:: i

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\drums, { Sympathy.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(2), 0.002, 0.05) * PinkNoise.ar(0.6 ! 2), \sympathy) }).play;
y = Sympathy(Ndef(\drums), \sympathy);
y.gui;
y.preset = Sympathy.presetNames.choose;
y.free; Ndef(\drums).clear;
::
